;; fault-shiftw-res.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-shiftw-res.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-shiftw-res.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "fault-shiftw-res.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-shiftw-res.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). The OQ-2 closure: D-SHIFTW-RESERVED marks the imm[5] != 0 *IW encodings RESERVED in" "this revision, and BOTH references were measured to raise illegal-instruction with tval = the" "word — the previous text's behavior — so the laboratory policy's observation agrees three-way" "while the model keeps the case's source classification (SEM-07). x2 is never written.")
(expectations (program "fault-shiftw-res.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (never_written "x2") (step (n 0) (insn "addi x1, x0, 7") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000000007"))) (derivation "The operand the reserved form would have shifted; an ordinary write so the reserved word is not the only step.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 1) (insn ".word 0x0210911B") (writes) (derivation "The word is slliw x2, x1, 1 with bit 25 (imm[5]) set: the *IW funct7 field is mask-pinned to zero in the generated table, so the word decodes to nothing — a RESERVED encoding (D-SHIFTW-RESERVED). The laboratory policy (D-RESERVED-DECODE) raises illegal-instruction with tval = the word; measured on sail-riscv 0.14 AND spike 1.1.1-dev as cause 0x02, tval 0x000000000210911B. x2 is never written — the negative observation an EXECUTING model would fail (it would write sext32(7 << 1) = 14).") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHIFTW-RESERVED: imm[5] != 0 is RESERVED); RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.2 (reserved decode is UNSPECIFIED) — decision D-RESERVED-DECODE")))
